# JSONotes — Phase 9: Schema-Agnostic Content Discovery Engine

## Context

JSONotes Phases 1–8 are complete.

Current architecture:

```text
JSON / Markdown
      ↓
Semantic Normalization
      ↓
Content Analysis
      ↓
Dynamic Measurement
      ↓
Layout Strategies
      ↓
Layout Recommendation
      ↓
User Preferences
      ↓
Theme Engine
      ↓
CanvasElement[]
      ↓
Editable Visual Notes
```

Current major limitation:

The semantic engine still understands content best when users follow JSONotes-specific field names such as:

```text
title
subtitle
definition
concepts
related
code
summary
interview
warning
memory
notes
```

Real users will provide arbitrary JSON:

```json
{
  "topic": "JavaScript Closures",
  "explanation": "A closure allows a function to retain access to its lexical scope.",
  "importantPoints": [
    "Uses lexical scoping",
    "Outer variables remain available"
  ],
  "exampleCode": "const outer = () => { let x = 1; return () => x; };",
  "thingsToAvoid": [
    "Retaining unnecessary large objects"
  ]
}
```

JSONotes should understand this without forcing users to rename their fields.

---

# PHASE 9 OBJECTIVE

Build a deterministic:

# Schema-Agnostic Content Discovery Engine

The engine should inspect arbitrary JSON structure and infer useful semantic blocks.

Target architecture:

```text
Raw JSON
   ↓
Known JSONotes Schema Detection
   ↓
Known fields processed directly
   +
Unknown fields
   ↓
Structure Discovery
   ↓
Field Signal Extraction
   ↓
Semantic Classification
   ↓
Confidence Scoring
   ↓
Strong Match → Semantic Type
Weak Match   → Generic Block
   ↓
SemanticDocument
   ↓
EXISTING PHASE 2–8 PIPELINE
```

CRITICAL:

Phase 9 MUST NOT use:

* AI
* LLMs
* OpenAI
* Gemini
* Claude
* embeddings
* vector databases
* network APIs
* external classification services

Everything must remain:

* local
* deterministic
* explainable
* fast
* backward compatible

Do NOT install AI SDKs.

