# 18. CODE DETECTION

Code must be detectable even without code-like field names.

Example:

```json
{
  "example": "const add = (a, b) => a + b;"
}
```

should likely become code.

Build:

```text
code-detection.ts
```

Use multiple deterministic signals.

Potential JS/TS indicators:

```text
const
let
var
function
=>
import
export
class
console.
;
{}
()
```

Potential Python:

```text
def
import
from
class
:
indentation
```

Potential SQL:

```text
SELECT
FROM
WHERE
INSERT
UPDATE
DELETE
JOIN
```

Potential HTML:

```text
<div>
<span>
<section>
<html>
```

Potential CSS:

```text
selector {
  property: value;
}
```

Do not classify based on one symbol alone.

---

# 19. CODE FALSE POSITIVE PROTECTION

This:

```text
Use {brackets} when describing placeholders.
```

must NOT become code simply because braces exist.

Require multiple supporting signals.

Code detector should return approximately:

```ts
interface CodeDetectionResult {
  isCode: boolean
  confidence: number
  language?: string
  reasons: string[]
}
```

---

# 20. LIGHTWEIGHT LANGUAGE HINT

Do not build a sophisticated language classifier.

Only return language when obvious.

Examples:

```text
const / let / =>
→ javascript

interface + const / type
→ typescript

def ...
→ python

SELECT ... FROM
→ sql

<div>
→ html

unknown
→ text
```

Existing explicit language metadata always wins.

---

# 21. STRING ARRAYS

Preserve arrays.

Example:

```json
{
  "advantages": [
    "Reusable",
    "Simple",
    "Fast"
  ]
}
```

Do NOT convert into one giant string during discovery.

Keep:

```text
["Reusable", "Simple", "Fast"]
```

Classification may decide:

```text
concept
summary
generic
```

depending on signals.

---

# 22. ARRAYS OF OBJECTS

Handle safely.

Example:

```json
{
  "algorithms": [
    {
      "name": "Bubble Sort",
      "complexity": "O(n²)"
    },
    {
      "name": "Merge Sort",
      "complexity": "O(n log n)"
    }
  ]
}
```

Do NOT:

```text
String(object)
```

Do NOT produce `[object Object]`.

For Phase 9 prefer a robust simple representation.

Recommended approach:

Represent the array as ONE structured generic block unless there is an obvious existing semantic representation.

Example:

```text
Algorithms

Bubble Sort
Complexity: O(n²)

Merge Sort
Complexity: O(n log n)
```

Keep original structured content where possible.

Do not build table rendering yet.

